Desktop selection and pane controls

Status: DONE
Milestone: Usable titlebar-free floating mirror
Dependencies: 02_NATIVE_CAPTURE
Purpose: Expose the live view without taking unnecessary screen space.

Tasks:
- [x] Add snipping selection with Escape cancellation.
- [x] Add borderless always-on-top pane with drag, resizing and context controls.
- [x] Add opacity and color-key picker/tolerance/softness controls.
- [x] Add hide/show recovery, tray menu and registered keyboard shortcuts.
- [x] Make errors visible and fully transparent/click-through panes recoverable.

Acceptance criteria:
- Normal view has no title bar and no permanent toolbar.
- User can reposition and recover a hidden or transparent pane.
- Picker samples captured source pixels, not an unrelated desktop screenshot.
- No click forwarding or interaction with source application.
- Selection and settings cancel safely without leaving an unclosable overlay.

Completion evidence:
- Native tests exercise selection mouse messages, actual slider/key-picker
  handlers, resized picker mapping, native drag/resize hit tests, edge snapping,
  click-through style, reset, hiding and cancellation.
- scripts\smoke-launch.ps1 passed normal startup, close-to-tray, controls recovery
  and clean exit. This is separate from the test mode that omits global hotkeys.
- Actual owned controls image docs\assets\controls.png inspected after fixing
  native checkbox text contrast and ensuring all child controls were repainted.
- Human physical interaction review and mixed-DPI/multi-monitor qualification
  remain pending. A normal pane has no caption/permanent toolbar.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-06: Recorded requested interaction scope.
- 2026-11-06: Completed the first one-pane desktop workflow and recovery surfaces.
